diff --git a/packages/ai/CHANGELOG.md b/packages/ai/CHANGELOG.md
index faca47f81c98e2ba5ced9324cf93b82ea5f71905..05b4346cc3546f288a7b23c7358a650c06a6506b 100644
--- a/packages/ai/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/packages/ai/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,13 @@
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Added `CursorExecHandlers.askQuestion`: Cursor's native `AskQuestion` is answered through the host as one `ask` form instead of being rejected: a fieldset per question, radios for one pick and checkboxes for many. A typed "Other" answer is sent as `freeform_text`, and repeated option labels take distinct form values so every option stays answerable. Hosts without the handler, and async questions, are still rejected ([#16497](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/16497) by [@morali](https://github.com/morali))
+- Added `CursorExecHandlers.subagent` and `subagentAwait`: Cursor's native `Task` runs on the host's subagents and returns their report instead of being rejected. Hosts without the handlers still reject it
+- Added host-run Cursor subagent types: `CursorExecHandlers.customSubagents` advertises them in the request context so Cursor's `Task` accepts the type, `artifactsFolder` names the folder `Task` may attach files from (`file_attachments`), and `CursorSubagentCall` carries the model Cursor picked (`modelId`) and the attached videos. `cursorVideos` (`CursorOptions.videos`) sends videos inline in the user message, which Gemini models read
+- Added mid-run live steering for Cursor: after each answered exec frame, queued user input and background-job completions go into the running turn as a `conversation_action` user message, recorded as answered once the server reports it appended (`user_message_appended`). Unconfirmed input returns to the caller for its next request, and a run that fails with input unconfirmed turns this off for the rest of the process. `LiveSteering.claim` takes `{ asides: true }`, and `LiveSteerClaim.acceptAnswered` reports input the model answered inside the response
+
 ## [18.18.4] - 2026-11-09
 
 ### Added
